<% content_for :title, "Cookie Policy — TrustShip" %>

<article class="print:bg-white">
  <header class="border-b border-gray-200 pb-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 md:text-4xl">Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-medium text-gray-500">Last updated: June 2025</p>
  </header>

  <nav class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-5 text-sm print:hidden" aria-label="Table of contents">
    <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900">On this page</p>
    <ol class="mt-4 grid list-decimal gap-x-8 gap-y-2 pl-5 text-gray-700 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <li class="pl-1"><a href="#introduction" class="text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-500">Introduction</a></li>
      <li class="pl-1"><a href="#what-are-cookies" class="text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-500">What Are Cookies</a></li>
      <li class="pl-1"><a href="#cookies-we-use" class="text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-500">Cookies We Use</a></li>
      <li class="pl-1"><a href="#cookies-we-do-not-use" class="text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-500">Cookies We Do NOT Use</a></li>
      <li class="pl-1"><a href="#third-party" class="text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-500">Third Party Cookies</a></li>
      <li class="pl-1"><a href="#managing" class="text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-500">Managing Cookies</a></li>
      <li class="pl-1"><a href="#consent" class="text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-500">Cookie Consent</a></li>
      <li class="pl-1"><a href="#future-changes" class="text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-500">Future Changes</a></li>
      <li class="pl-1"><a href="#contact" class="text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-500">Contact</a></li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <div class="mt-12 space-y-12 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
    <section id="introduction" class="scroll-mt-24">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">1. Introduction</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        TrustShip uses cookies to keep you logged in and keep the platform secure. That&apos;s pretty much it.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        We don&apos;t use advertising cookies. We don&apos;t track you across the internet. We don&apos;t sell cookie data to anyone.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        This page explains exactly what cookies we use and why.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="what-are-cookies" class="scroll-mt-24">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">2. What Are Cookies</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Cookies are small text files stored on your device when you visit a website. They help websites remember you between page visits.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">There are different types:</p>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li><strong class="font-semibold text-gray-800">Essential cookies</strong> — needed for the website to function</li>
        <li><strong class="font-semibold text-gray-800">Analytics cookies</strong> — track how you use the site</li>
        <li><strong class="font-semibold text-gray-800">Advertising cookies</strong> — track you across websites for ads</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 font-medium text-gray-800">
        TrustShip only uses essential cookies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="cookies-we-use" class="scroll-mt-24">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">3. Cookies We Use</h2>

      <div class="mt-6 rounded-xl border border-indigo-200 bg-indigo-50 px-4 py-4 text-center text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-950 sm:text-base print:border-gray-200 print:bg-gray-50">
        Only 3 essential cookies — all required for TrustShip to work.
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200 print:border-gray-300">
        <table class="min-w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 bg-gray-50">
              <th scope="col" class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">Cookie name</th>
              <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">Purpose</th>
              <th scope="col" class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">Type</th>
              <th scope="col" class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">Duration</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100">
            <tr class="bg-white">
              <td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-gray-800 sm:text-sm">_trustship_session</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Keeps you logged in to your account</td>
              <td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-3">Essential</td>
              <td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-3">Until browser closes or 2 weeks if remember me selected</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50/80">
              <td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-gray-800 sm:text-sm">authenticity_token</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Protects against CSRF security attacks</td>
              <td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-3">Essential</td>
              <td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-3">Session only</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-white">
              <td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-gray-800 sm:text-sm">flash_*</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Shows success/error messages after actions</td>
              <td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-3">Essential</td>
              <td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-3">Session only</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-6 font-medium text-gray-800">
        That&apos;s it. Three cookies. All essential. None optional.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="cookies-we-do-not-use" class="scroll-mt-24">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50/90 px-5 py-6 text-emerald-950 print:border-gray-300 print:bg-gray-50 print:text-gray-800">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-emerald-950 print:text-gray-900">4. Cookies We Do NOT Use</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          We want to be clear about what we do not do:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-none space-y-2">
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true">❌</span><span>No Google Analytics or any analytics tracking</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true">❌</span><span>No Facebook Pixel or Meta tracking</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true">❌</span><span>No advertising or retargeting cookies</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true">❌</span><span>No third party tracking of any kind</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true">❌</span><span>No heatmap or session recording tools</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true">❌</span><span>No A/B testing cookies</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true">❌</span><span>No data sold to advertisers</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-6 font-medium text-emerald-900 print:text-gray-900">
          When we say we respect your privacy — we mean it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="third-party" class="scroll-mt-24">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">5. Third Party Cookies</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        TrustShip itself sets no third party cookies.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        However when you use TrustShip, some third party services we integrate with may set their own cookies:
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        <strong class="font-semibold text-gray-800">Razorpay</strong> — payment processing. When you make a payment via Razorpay, they may set cookies governed by their own cookie policy.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        <strong class="font-semibold text-gray-800">Meta WhatsApp</strong> — the WhatsApp connection flow may involve Meta&apos;s own cookies governed by Meta&apos;s cookie policy.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        We have no control over third party cookies. Please review their respective policies for details.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="managing" class="scroll-mt-24">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">6. Managing Cookies</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Since TrustShip only uses essential cookies, disabling them will affect how the platform works:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li>Disabling session cookie — you will be logged out every time you close the browser</li>
        <li>Disabling authenticity token — forms and actions will not work correctly for security reasons</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4">You can manage cookies in your browser settings:</p>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li>Chrome: Settings → Privacy → Cookies</li>
        <li>Firefox: Settings → Privacy → Cookies</li>
        <li>Safari: Preferences → Privacy → Cookies</li>
        <li>Edge: Settings → Privacy → Cookies</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4">
        <strong class="font-semibold text-gray-800">Note:</strong> Blocking essential cookies may break TrustShip functionality.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="consent" class="scroll-mt-24">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">7. Cookie Consent</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Because TrustShip only uses strictly essential cookies that are required for the platform to function — we do not show a cookie consent banner.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Essential cookies do not require consent under most privacy regulations as they are necessary for the service you have requested.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        If we ever introduce non-essential cookies in future, we will update this policy and add a proper consent mechanism.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="future-changes" class="scroll-mt-24">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">8. Future Changes</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">If TrustShip introduces analytics or other non-essential cookies in future:</p>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li>This policy will be updated</li>
        <li>A cookie consent banner will be added</li>
        <li>You will have full control over non-essential cookies</li>
        <li>We will notify users via email before changes take effect</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="contact" class="scroll-mt-24">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">9. Contact</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">Questions about our cookie policy?</p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        <strong class="font-semibold text-gray-800">Email:</strong> <%= support_email %>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        We will respond within 3 business days.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <p class="mt-14 border-t border-gray-200 pt-10 print:mt-8">
    <%= link_to "← Back to Home", root_path, class: "text-sm font-medium text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-500" %>
  </p>
</article>
